    "rule": "Pass only if all three hold on the test window for the headline model, which is picked on the validation window as the personalised candidate (item_knn, svd, svd_ips) with the highest NDCG@10 against held-out clicks: (1) the 95% paired bootstrap interval over users on its NDCG@10 minus popularity's has a lower bound above zero; (2) the 95% paired interval on its true like rate at 10 minus popularity's has a lower bound above zero, where the true like rate is known only because this is a simulation; (3) across all seven models, the Spearman correlation between NDCG@10 on held-out clicks and the true like rate is at least 0.80, meaning the offline metric can be trusted to choose between models. The 0.80 bar is an assumption fixed before results.",
